# The data tree stays out of git: bronze DICOM (138 GB), silver volumes and the gold
# banks derived from them. One rule covers every layer and every future dataset
# -- the previous list of per-experiment folder names had to be edited each time a run
# produced a new directory. Layout and rebuild commands: config.py.
#
# `data/*` rather than `data/`, because git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, and the demo cases below have to stay versioned.
data/*
!data/gold/
data/gold/*
!data/gold/demo_cases/
data/gold/demo_cases/*
# The three demo cases are the exception. Each is a 25-slice slab around one pinned
# axial slice (4-5 MB, against ~30 MB for the full volume) taken from a public, already
# de-identified TCIA study (Duke-Breast-Cancer-MRI), so there is no PHI to leak, and
# shipping them is what makes `git clone` + `pip install` enough to replay the demo.
# The slab, rather than the single slice, is what the slider and the MIP view need.
# Rebuild: scripts/make_demo_cases.py.
!data/gold/demo_cases/*.npz

# Logs
*.log
logs/
download.log

