# Trained artefacts. Checkpoints are large and most are throwaway, so the tree is
# excluded and the two runs the demo and the README depend on are re-included by name.
models/*

# The DCE-MRI run serving the demo is the exception to "no artefacts in git": its
# checkpoint and metrics ARE versioned, so `git clone` + `pip install` is enough to
# replay the demo on another machine. Everything else in the folder stays out.
!models/dce_mri_p2_negfix/
models/dce_mri_p2_negfix/*
!models/dce_mri_p2_negfix/unet_best.pt
!models/dce_mri_p2_negfix/segmentation_metrics.csv
!models/dce_mri_p2_negfix/segmentation_test_metrics.csv
!models/dce_mri_p2_negfix/eval_report.json
!models/dce_mri_p2_negfix/eval_per_patient.csv

# Slice classifier (imaging.sliceclf): the checkpoint is 2.4 MB and its metrics are
# the evidence behind the localisation claims, so both are versioned.
!models/sliceclf/
models/sliceclf/*
!models/sliceclf/sliceclf_best.pt
!models/sliceclf/sliceclf_metrics.csv
!models/sliceclf/sliceclf_test_metrics.json

# Exam classifier (code removed 2026-09-20, the project now being MRI-only): the
# measurement artefacts stay versioned as the evidence of the published negative results. The reports
# are the evidence for a *negative* result (DOCUMENTATION.md section 4.7), the
# checkpoint is a model that detects none of its 56 held-out cancers. _bag32 is a
# second measurement (larger MIL bag, a lead from section 4.7) that did not help.
!models/examclf/
models/examclf/*
!models/examclf/cv_report.json
!models/examclf/cv_predictions.csv
!models/examclf/cv_report_bag32.json
!models/examclf/cv_predictions_bag32.csv
# Same rule for the two leads measured on 2026-09-14 (DOCUMENTATION.md 4.8, 4.10): the reports
# are the evidence that a warm-started encoder and a relative bag score do not help,
# and the fold-0 checkpoints beside them are not versioned for the same reason as above.
!models/examclf/warmstart5/
models/examclf/warmstart5/*
!models/examclf/warmstart5/cv_report.json
!models/examclf/warmstart5/cv_predictions.csv
!models/examclf/relative/
models/examclf/relative/*
!models/examclf/relative/cv_report.json
!models/examclf/relative/cv_predictions.csv

